<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jethwa dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jethwas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jethwas are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> clan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, and one of the oldest ruling families of the region. Their tradition traces their power far back; historically they held western Saurashtra from seats at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghumli">Ghumli</a> and later Ranpur and Chhaya, and from 1785 at Porbandar. Their state of Porbandar joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1948, and its capital is known as the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Mahatma Gandhi</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Origins</h2><p>The Jethwas claim descent from Makardhwaja, son of Hanuman, through his son Mod-dhwaja and grandson Jethi-dhwaja, from whom they take their name, and they worship Hanuman as their chosen deity. His image stood at the centre of the Porbandar coat of arms and on the merchant navy flag the state adopted in 1923. Scholars have proposed other origins: Captain Wilberforce Bell thought their ancestors probably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scythians">Scythians</a> from the north, while Gaurishankar Ojha held them to be probably a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parihar">Pratihars</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a>. Some have linked them to the Saindhavas, who repulsed naval raids from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> coast in the 7th century.</p><p>Close ties bound the family to the Mer people, who supported the Jethwas in war and peace. When a Rana of Porbandar came to the throne, the leader of the Mers cut the tip of his own little finger and marked the new ruler's forehead with his blood.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">History</h2><p>Family tradition dates the founding to about 620 under Shil Kumar Jethwa, but historians generally hold that the Jethwas came into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> and Kutch and established their rule around 900, with Morvi as their capital. They spread westward, took Dwarka from the Chawdas, and by the time of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a> controlled the west and north of Kathiawar. Sangaji, who ruled from 1120 to 1150, defeated Virdhaval Vaghela near Morvi in 1125 and took from him the title of Rana, which the family kept until the last Rana died in 1979.</p><p>Morvi fell to the army of Qutb-ud-din Aibak in 1193. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghumli">Ghumli</a> then served as capital until 1313, when Jam Barmaniyaji Jadeja defeated Rana Bhanji Jethwa and left the town in ruins. Around 1525–35 Jam Raval conquered most of Halar, including Nagnah, which became Nawanagar, opening an enmity with the Jadeja Jams that lasted some three centuries. In 1671 Rana Vikmatji Khimoji Jethwa took Porbandar from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> and built a fort there, and in 1807 the Jethwas allied with the British. Porbandar became a 13-gun salute state.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Legacy</h2><p>The Navlakha Temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghumli">Ghumli</a>, built by Jethwa rulers in the 12th century and dedicated to the Sun god, is the oldest sun temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, on a base of 45.72 by 30.48 m. Nearby stands the ruined Vikia Vav, one of the largest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stepwell">stepwells</a> of the state. At Porbandar the rulers built the Darbargarh, the Sartanji Choro summer pavilion and, in the late 19th century, the Daria Mahal, now a college. Uttamchand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Gandhi</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karamchand-gandhi">Karamchand Gandhi</a>, grandfather and father of Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi, served as Dewan to the Rana of Porbandar.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Jethwa dynasty” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Jethwa</b> Rajputs are among the oldest ruling clans of Saurashtra, and tradition gives their rule an early date.</blockquote><a href="/state/porbandar-state">Porbandar State</a></li><li><blockquote>Ghumli later became a seat of the <b>Jethwa</b> rulers of the region.</blockquote><a href="/state/saindhava-dynasty">Saindhava dynasty</a></li></ul></section>
